scenario no_cut over lis
  tally 2
  from 2022-01-01
  note "A-01's without: the July 2022 cut never made, PIT-3 v2 for 2022 on, advances too (questions.md A-01: without the cut). The what-if keeps PIT-3 v2 in force: its version is known 2022-07-01, the day v3 would have entered into force, so the asks of A-01 (as known 2024-04-30) and A-03 (as known 2023-01-31) see it; dated with v3's publication, 2022-06-14, its table ties with v3's, which the reference interpreter refuses (fault F5). It sets no_cut_on, so the advances are computed again (the rule nocut of y_adv, tax.tally), not read from the yearly information."

version nocut_on
  cite questions
  governs 2022-01-01..
  known 2022-07-01
  enters 2022-01-01
  replace pit3_rate: [0, 120000] = 0.18 "PIT-3 v2 .1, kept in force: 18 % of the base up to 120 000.00 DUK"
  replace pit3_rate: (120000, inf) = 0.33 "PIT-3 v2 .1, kept in force: 33 % of the part above 120 000.00 DUK"
  replace pit3_reducing = 5400.00 "PIT-3 v2 .2, kept in force"
  replace no_cut_on = true "questions.md A-01: without the cut, advances too"
